Vikram and Betal: The Grateful Boy (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100135

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a boy who received help from many people,” said Betal. “But he never said thank you.”

One day, he got lost in a forest.

A kind man helped him find his way home.

This time, the boy said, “Thank you for helping me.”

The man smiled and said, “Gratitude makes kindness meaningful.”

The boy thought about it.

He realized he had never thanked anyone before.

From that day, he began to thank everyone who helped him.

People were happy to help him even more.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what did the boy learn?”

Vikram replied, “He learned the value of gratitude.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Always be thankful for help.
